<h1>mcp-librarian Wiki</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">Comprehensive documentation for the self-growing knowledge library for AI coding agents.</p>

    <h2 id="what-is-mcp-librarian">What is mcp-librarian?</h2>

    <p>mcp-librarian is an MCP (Model Context Protocol) server that gives AI coding agents a persistent, searchable knowledge library. It exposes {{ versions.librarian.tools }} tools over the MCP protocol &mdash; {{ versions.librarian.localTools }} local and {{ versions.librarian.networkTools }} explicitly labelled network tools &mdash; that let agents find existing skills, research new topics from the web, install community-curated packs, and create permanent knowledge, all without leaving the editor. Zero dependencies, {{ versions.librarian.license }}.</p>

    <p>The core design principle is zero friction. When your agent starts a session, it sees a catalog of available skills. When you ask about REST APIs, security patterns, or database optimization, the agent automatically searches the library for relevant knowledge. Ask about something the library does not cover and <code>research_topic</code> pulls it from authoritative web sources so it becomes a permanent skill; the next time anyone asks, the answer is instant.</p>

    <p>The second principle is that a knowledge library is a supply chain, so it gets treated like one. Skills are Ed25519-signed on write and integrity-checked on load, all content passes a prompt-injection guard, and every network path is SSRF-hardened and credential-scoped.</p>

    <h2 id="key-concepts">Key Concepts</h2>

    <h3>Skills</h3>
    <p>A skill is a Markdown file with YAML frontmatter that contains structured knowledge on a specific topic. Skills are indexed at the section level using BM25 full-text search, so agents retrieve the narrowest useful slice of knowledge rather than entire documents. Skills are cryptographically signed with Ed25519 to detect tampering.</p>

    <h3>Packs</h3>
    <p>A pack is a collection of related skills bundled together with a <code>pack.json</code> manifest. The community repository hosts 9 curated packs covering security, API design, Git, TypeScript, Docker, PostgreSQL, testing, writing, and prompt engineering. One tool call installs a pack.</p>

    <h3>Auto-Research</h3>
    <p>When no skill matches a query, mcp-librarian searches the web, scores sources by authority (official docs rank highest), fetches content from the top results, and returns research material for the agent to synthesize into a permanent skill. The library grows organically from real questions.</p>

    <h3>MCP Protocol</h3>
    <p>MCP (Model Context Protocol) is the communication layer between AI agents and tool servers. mcp-librarian speaks MCP over stdio, which means it works with any MCP-compatible client: Claude Code, Cursor, Windsurf, or local models via Ollama and LM Studio. The server is model-agnostic -- it does not care what model is on the other end.</p>

